  "outcome": {
    "ok": true,
    "turn_id": "d09_final_relationship:r3:t3",
    "narration": "Iris stood near one of the empty beds, the sparse floor stretching out around them both. The wooden cabinets on the far wall sat shut and bare. Light came flat and plain through the tower stone, catching nothing of interest.\n\nShe looked at Nicco for a long moment, then drew her elbows closer to her sides.\n\n\"I don't have much to compare it to,\" she said. Her voice carried no particular warmth, but no edge either — just the flat sound of someone weighing words with little practice at it. \"You asked. You waited. That's more than I'd have expected, honestly.\" She paused, glancing toward the spiral stair and then back. \"Whether it stays that way when something actually matters — that I can't tell you yet.\"",
